.policy "tanstack-query-practice-same-key-different-query-fn" revision 1
.description "Give each query key one query function: two queries with the same key and different fetchers share one cache entry, so one of them gets the other's data."
.language typescript
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.ts", "**/*.mts", "**/*.cts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.mjs", "**/*.cjs"
.scope exclude "**/*.test.*", "**/*.spec.*", "**/*.cy.*", "**/__tests__/**", "**/test/**", "**/tests/**", "**/e2e/**", "**/__mocks__/**", "**/*.stories.*", "**/*.story.*", "**/__stories__/**", "**/__fixtures__/**", "**/fixtures/**", "**/node_modules/**", "**/dist/**", "**/build/**", "**/out/**", "**/.next/**", "**/coverage/**", "**/vendor/**", "**/.venv/**", "**/.yarn/**", "**/generated/**", "**/__generated__/**", "**/*.generated.*", "**/*.gen.*", "**/*.min.js", "**/*.d.ts"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. TanStack Query caches by key alone: whichever query with a key runs first fills
// the entry, and every other observer of that key reads it. Two query definitions with the same key and different
// query functions therefore hand one component the other's data (missing fields, another shape), and each refetch
// overwrites the other. @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query sees one file; this rule joins the query definitions of a
// package across its files. Each file states its definitions by its path and the line of their queryFn, with their
// templates and fetchers, and the pairing joins those values alone (decision 0677).
// A query definition is an object literal with a `queryKey` and a `queryFn` (useQuery, useSuspenseQuery,
// queryOptions, useQueries entries, prefetchQuery, fetchQuery, ensureQueryData, a wrapper hook's options). Its key
// template is the key array with string, number and keyword elements kept, an object element as its sorted property
// names (`{boardId, modified}`, `...` for a spread: the key hash sorts keys) and every other element `*`
// (['user', *]), or a key factory call by the declaration it calls with its arguments read the same way
// (`<module>#userKeys.detail(*)`: tsx/names' symbol for the factory's root, through imports, re-exports and `const
// a = b` aliases, so two files' own `listKey` functions are two factories and an import of one is that one). A
// definition inside a `createQueryKeyStore`/`createQueryKeys` object of @lukemorales/query-key-factory has the key
// the library caches: its property path in front of its queryKey (['users', 'detail', *]). Its fetchers are the
// callees its queryFn calls or names (an aliased import by the name it imports, any other name by its dotted text,
// the global `fetch`), the callees of a function of the same file it calls (one hop), and for each call a string
// first argument (`fetch('/api/user/*')`).
// It reports both definitions of a pair in one package (the nearest package.json), both plain or both infinite,
// with one key template and fetchers that have nothing in common:
//   useQuery({ queryKey: ['user', id], queryFn: () => getUser(id) })                       a.ts
//   useQuery({ queryKey: ['user', id], queryFn: () => getUserWithInvoices(id) })           b.ts: both reported
//   useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: () => fetch('/api/todos').then(r => r.json()) })
//   useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: () => fetch('/api/todos/done').then(...) })   both reported
// It leaves alone:
//   - a definition with no queryFn (an observer of an entry another query fills) or a shorthand `{ queryKey,
//     queryFn }`, and one whose key is a variable, has a spread, or (an array) has no string element;
//   - keys whose object elements or factory arguments differ: ['boards', { teamId }] and ['boards', { boardId }];
//     calls of two factories of one name (each file's own `const listKey = …`); and two entries of a
//     query-key-factory store with one returned queryKey (the library puts each entry's path in front of it);
//   - two definitions sharing a fetcher: the same callee with a different `select` or other arguments, a direct
//     reference and a call (`queryFn: getUser` and `() => getUser(id)`), the same function under another import
//     name, a same-file helper that calls it; the same callee with string arguments in common, or one not a string;
//   - a queryFn that calls a parameter of an enclosing function (a wrapper hook's fetcher), or only locals and
//     globals other than fetch (its fetcher is unknown);
//   - a plain and an infinite query (tanstack-query-practice-infinite-and-plain-share-key reports those), and two
//     definitions in different packages of a monorepo (different apps have different QueryClients);
//   - a prefetch (`fetchQuery`, `prefetchQuery`, `ensureQueryData` and their infinite forms) in a file that calls
//     TanStack Query's `dehydrate`: a server render filling the cache it hands to the browser, whose fetcher is the
//     server's way to the data the browser's query fetches (`ssrApi.getDashboard` and `getDashboard`), so the two
//     have different fetchers by design.
// Gaps: two wrappers around one endpoint in different files (`getUser` and `api.users.get`) are different
// fetchers; the same fetcher with a transform outside `select` is the same one; `*` elements are not compared, so
// ['user', id] and ['user', slug] meet; the v3 positional form `useQuery(key, fn)` is not read; a .ts and a .tsx
// definition are not paired until the engine joins the two lanes; two definitions whose queryFn start on one line (a
// one-line `useQueries`) are one, by path and line, and are not paired; a factory imported from a module tsx/names
// cannot resolve is read by the name it imports, and so meets only other calls of that name the same way; a
// query-key-factory definition under `contextQueries` or returned from a block body has no template; a server
// prefetch whose file does not itself call dehydrate is paired as any definition is, and one whose fetcher returns
// another shape than the browser's query is not reported.

#include "tsx/names.rerail"

.violation SameKeyDifferentQueryFn(at: node, key: symbol, other: symbol, oline: number) "Another query in this package uses the key {key} with a different queryFn ({other}:{oline}). TanStack Query caches by key alone, so whichever runs first fills the entry and the other component gets that function's data, of the wrong shape. Give one of them its own key by appending an element (such as 'with-invoices'), so invalidations of the shared prefix still reach it, or share one queryOptions and derive the difference with `select`. Leave it if both functions return the same data for the same key values; then call one shared fetcher from both."
SameKeyDifferentQueryFn(f, t, b, lb) :- skd_at(a, p, la), skd_other(p, la, b, lb), skd_prop(a, "queryFn", f),
    skd_key(a, t).

// ---- query definitions -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// skd_raw(o, k, v): object literal o has a pair `k: v`, k queryKey or queryFn.
.decl skd_raw(o: node, k: symbol, v: node)
skd_raw(o, "queryKey", v) :- kind(p, "pair"), field(p, "key", n), text(n, "queryKey"), field(p, "value", v),
    child(o, p, _), kind(o, "object").
skd_raw(o, "queryFn", v) :- kind(p, "pair"), field(p, "key", n), text(n, "queryFn"), field(p, "value", v),
    child(o, p, _), kind(o, "object").
// skd_prop(o, k, x): the value without parentheses, `as const` and `satisfies T`.
.decl skd_wrap(v: node, x: node)
skd_wrap(v, v) :- skd_raw(_, _, v).
skd_wrap(v, x) :- skd_wrap(v, w), (kind(w, "parenthesized_expression") ; kind(w, "as_expression") ;
    kind(w, "satisfies_expression")), child(w, x, 0).
.decl skd_prop(o: node, k: symbol, x: node)
skd_prop(o, k, x) :- skd_raw(o, k, v), skd_wrap(v, x), !kind(x, "parenthesized_expression"), !kind(x, "as_expression"),
    !kind(x, "satisfies_expression").
// skd_site(o): o has both.
.decl skd_site(o: node)
skd_site(o) :- skd_prop(o, "queryKey", _), skd_prop(o, "queryFn", _).
// skd_kind(o, k): "infinite" for an infinite query's options (a page param option, or an argument of
// useInfiniteQuery, infiniteQueryOptions, prefetchInfiniteQuery, ...), else "plain".
.decl skd_infinite(o: node)
skd_infinite(o) :- skd_site(o), kind(p, "pair"), child(o, p, _), field(p, "key", n),
    (text(n, "initialPageParam") ; text(n, "getNextPageParam") ; text(n, "getPreviousPageParam")).
skd_infinite(o) :- skd_site(o), child(al, o, _), kind(al, "arguments"), field(c, "arguments", al),
    field(c, "function", g), (kind(g, "identifier"), text(g, x) ; kind(g, "member_expression"), field(g, "property", pr),
    text(pr, x)), glob("*Infinite*", x).
.decl skd_kind(o: node, k: symbol)
skd_kind(o, "infinite") :- skd_infinite(o).
skd_kind(o, "plain") :- skd_site(o), !skd_infinite(o).

// ---- key templates -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// skd_elem(a, e, i): element e of key array a, or argument e of key factory call arguments a; comments left out.
.decl skd_elem(a: node, e: node, i: number)
skd_elem(a, e, i) :- skd_site(o), skd_prop(o, "queryKey", a), kind(a, "array"), child(a, e, i), !kind(e, "comment").
skd_elem(a, e, i) :- skd_site(o), skd_prop(o, "queryKey", c), kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "arguments", a),
    child(a, e, i), !kind(e, "comment").
// skd_tok(e, t): how element e reads in a template.
.decl skd_tok(e: node, t: symbol)
skd_tok(e, cat("'", v, "'")) :- skd_elem(_, e, _), (kind(e, "string") ; kind(e, "template_string")), str(e, v).
skd_tok(e, t) :- skd_elem(_, e, _), kind(e, "template_string"), !str(e, _), text(e, s),
    t = @replace_all(s, "\\$\\{[^}]*\\}", "*").
skd_tok(e, s) :- skd_elem(_, e, _), kind(e, k), (k = "number" ; k = "true" ; k = "false" ; k = "null" ;
    k = "undefined"), text(e, s).
skd_tok(e, "*") :- skd_elem(_, e, _), kind(e, k), k != "string", k != "template_string", k != "number", k != "true",
    k != "false", k != "null", k != "undefined", k != "spread_element", k != "object".
// An object element reads as its sorted property names, `...` for a spread: the key hash sorts an object's keys, so
// ['boards', { teamId }] and ['boards', { boardId }] never meet. Values are not compared.
skd_tok(e, cat("{", s, "}")) :- skd_elem(_, e, _), kind(e, "object"), s = join x by x sep ", " : { skd_okey(e, x) }.
.decl skd_okey(e: node, x: symbol)
skd_okey(e, x) :- skd_elem(_, e, _), kind(e, "object"), child(e, p, _), kind(p, "pair"), field(p, "key", n),
    (kind(n, "string"), str(n, x) ; !kind(n, "string"), text(n, x)).
skd_okey(e, x) :- skd_elem(_, e, _), kind(e, "object"), child(e, p, _), kind(p, "shorthand_property_identifier"),
    text(p, x).
skd_okey(e, "...") :- skd_elem(_, e, _), kind(e, "object"), child(e, p, _), kind(p, "spread_element").
// skd_key(o, t): o's key template. An array with a spread or no string element has none.
.decl skd_key(o: node, t: symbol)
skd_key(o, cat("[", s, "]")) :- skd_prop(o, "queryKey", a), kind(a, "array"), !skd_in_qkf(o),
    count : { skd_elem(a, e, _), kind(e, "spread_element") } = 0,
    count : { skd_elem(a, e, _), kind(e, k), (k = "string" ; k = "template_string") } > 0,
    s = join t by i sep ", " : { skd_elem(a, e, i), skd_tok(e, t) }.
// A key factory call: `userKeys.detail(id)` is the factory it calls and its arguments read as array elements do, so
// `daily({ ...p, groupBy })` and `daily({ employeeId })` are two templates.
skd_key(o, cat(h, "(", s, ")")) :- skd_site(o), skd_prop(o, "queryKey", c), kind(c, "call_expression"),
    !skd_in_qkf(o), field(c, "function", g), skd_fac(g, h), field(c, "arguments", a),
    count : { skd_elem(a, e, _), kind(e, "spread_element") } = 0,
    s = join t by i sep ", " : { skd_elem(a, e, i), skd_tok(e, t) }.
// A query-key-factory definition: its path, then its queryKey's elements (none for `queryKey: null` or `[]`).
skd_key(o, cat("[", p, ", ", s, "]")) :- skd_qkf_def(o, p), skd_prop(o, "queryKey", a), kind(a, "array"),
    count : { skd_elem(a, e, _), kind(e, "spread_element") } = 0, count : { skd_elem(a, _, _) } > 0,
    s = join t by i sep ", " : { skd_elem(a, e, i), skd_tok(e, t) }.
skd_key(o, cat("[", p, "]")) :- skd_qkf_def(o, p), skd_prop(o, "queryKey", a), kind(a, "array"),
    count : { skd_elem(a, _, _) } = 0.
skd_key(o, cat("[", p, "]")) :- skd_qkf_def(o, p), skd_prop(o, "queryKey", a), kind(a, "null").

// skd_fac(g, h): key factory callee g (`listKey`, `userKeys.detail`) is h: the symbol of the declaration its root
// names (tsx/names' sym_of, `module#name`: a top-level declaration of this file, or an import followed through
// re-exports to its module), after `const a = b` aliases, then the rest of the dotted path. Two files' own
// `listKey` functions are two factories; `listKey = customListKey` and an import of customListKey are one. A root
// sym_of cannot name is its import's imported name (`import { a as b }` is a, a namespace or default import its
// local name), else, declared inside a function, its file, name and line. A parameter or a global names none.
.decl skd_fac(g: node, h: symbol)
skd_fac(g, cat(q, substr(s, n, strlen(s) - n))) :- skd_fac_root(g, r), skd_fac_name(r, q), text(r, rt),
    n = strlen(rt), skd_path(g, s).
.decl skd_fac_root(g: node, r: node)
skd_fac_root(g, g) :- skd_site(o), skd_prop(o, "queryKey", c), kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", g),
    kind(g, "identifier").
skd_fac_root(g, r) :- skd_site(o), skd_prop(o, "queryKey", c), kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", g),
    kind(g, "member_expression"), field(g, "object", m), skd_root_up(m, r).
// skd_alias(r, x): root r, or the identifier a `const`/`let` alias on the way from r binds it to.
.decl skd_alias(r: node, x: node)
skd_alias(r, r) :- skd_fac_root(_, r).
skd_alias(r, x) :- skd_alias(r, y), ref_site(y, sp), binding_value(sp, x), kind(x, "identifier").
.decl skd_aliased(y: node)
skd_aliased(y) :- skd_alias(_, y), ref_site(y, sp), binding_value(sp, x), kind(x, "identifier").
.decl skd_fac_name(r: node, q: symbol)
skd_fac_name(r, q) :- skd_alias(r, y), !skd_aliased(y), sym_of(y, q).
skd_fac_name(r, x) :- skd_alias(r, y), !skd_aliased(y), !sym_of(y, _), ref_site(y, sp), import_binding(sp, _, _, x),
    x != "*", x != "default".
skd_fac_name(r, x) :- skd_alias(r, y), !skd_aliased(y), !sym_of(y, _), ref_site(y, sp), import_binding(sp, x, _, i),
    (i = "*" ; i = "default").
skd_fac_name(r, cat(p, "#", x, "@", to_string(l))) :- skd_alias(r, y), !skd_aliased(y), !sym_of(y, _),
    ref_site(y, sp), site_form(sp, f), f != "import", f != "param", text(y, x), docof(y, d), doc(d, p, _),
    line(sp, l).

// skd_in_qkf(o): definition o is inside a `createQueryKeyStore(…)` or `createQueryKeys(…)` call of
// @lukemorales/query-key-factory, which caches it under its path followed by its queryKey: in
//   createQueryKeyStore({ users: { detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: [id], queryFn }) } })
//   createQueryKeys('users', { detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: [id], queryFn }) })
// the key is ['users', 'detail', id]. skd_qkf_def(o, p) gives a definition reached through that path its prefix p
// (`'users', 'detail'`); one under contextQueries, or returned from a block body, has none.
.decl skd_qkf_call(c: node, x: symbol)
skd_qkf_call(c, x) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", g), kind(g, "identifier"), ref_site(g, sp),
    import_binding(sp, _, "@lukemorales/query-key-factory", x), (x = "createQueryKeyStore" ; x = "createQueryKeys").
.decl skd_in_qkf(o: node)
skd_in_qkf(o) :- skd_site(o), skd_qkf_call(c, _), within(o, c).
// skd_pname(n, k): a property name, `detail` or `'detail'`.
.decl skd_pname(n: node, k: symbol)
skd_pname(n, k) :- field(pr, "key", n), kind(pr, "pair"), (kind(n, "string"), str(n, k) ; !kind(n, "string"), text(n, k)).
// skd_qkf_schema(s, p): object s holds entries whose keys start with p.
.decl skd_qkf_schema(s: node, p: symbol)
skd_qkf_schema(s, cat("'", k, "'")) :- skd_qkf_call(c, "createQueryKeyStore"), field(c, "arguments", al),
    child(al, st, _), kind(st, "object"), child(st, pr, _), kind(pr, "pair"), field(pr, "key", n), skd_pname(n, k),
    field(pr, "value", s), kind(s, "object").
skd_qkf_schema(s, cat("'", k, "'")) :- skd_qkf_call(c, "createQueryKeys"), field(c, "arguments", al),
    child(al, n, _), kind(n, "string"), str(n, k), child(al, s, _), kind(s, "object").
// skd_qkf_entry(v, p): v is an entry's value, keyed by p.
.decl skd_qkf_entry(v: node, p: symbol)
skd_qkf_entry(v, cat(p, ", '", k, "'")) :- skd_qkf_schema(s, p), child(s, pr, _), kind(pr, "pair"), field(pr, "key", n),
    skd_pname(n, k), field(pr, "value", v).
// skd_qkf_val(v, x): x is v without parentheses, `as const` and `satisfies T`, or the expression an arrow returns.
.decl skd_qkf_val(v: node, x: node)
skd_qkf_val(v, v) :- skd_qkf_entry(v, _).
skd_qkf_val(v, x) :- skd_qkf_val(v, w), (kind(w, "parenthesized_expression") ; kind(w, "as_expression") ;
    kind(w, "satisfies_expression")), child(w, x, 0).
skd_qkf_val(v, x) :- skd_qkf_val(v, w), kind(w, "arrow_function"), field(w, "body", x).
.decl skd_qkf_def(o: node, p: symbol)
skd_qkf_def(o, p) :- skd_qkf_entry(v, p), skd_qkf_val(v, o), kind(o, "object"), skd_site(o).

// ---- fetchers ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// skd_callee(g, f): g is the callee of a call in queryFn f, f itself when it names a function, the callee of a call
// in a function of the same file that f calls (one hop, f the function), or the callee of a key factory call (f
// the call).
.decl skd_callee(g: node, f: node)
skd_callee(f, f) :- skd_prop(_, "queryFn", f), (kind(f, "identifier") ; kind(f, "member_expression")).
skd_callee(g, f) :- skd_prop(_, "queryFn", f), (kind(f, "arrow_function") ; kind(f, "function_expression") ;
    kind(f, "call_expression")), kind(c, "call_expression"), (c = f ; within(c, f)), field(c, "function", g).
skd_callee(g, c) :- skd_prop(_, "queryKey", c), kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", g).
skd_callee(g, def) :- skd_hop(_, def), kind(c, "call_expression"), within(c, def), field(c, "function", g).
// skd_hop(f, def): queryFn f calls or names a function def declared in its own file outside f (`fetchActual`
// calling the service a sibling query calls directly): def's callees are f's fetchers too.
.decl skd_hop(f: node, def: node)
skd_hop(f, def) :- skd_prop(_, "queryFn", f), skd_callee(g, f), kind(g, "identifier"), ref_site(g, sp), !within(sp, f),
    skd_fndef(sp, def).
.decl skd_fndef(sp: node, def: node)
skd_fndef(sp, sp) :- kind(sp, "function_declaration").
skd_fndef(sp, v) :- kind(sp, "variable_declarator"), field(sp, "value", v),
    (kind(v, "arrow_function") ; kind(v, "function_expression")).
// skd_root(g, r): r is the leftmost identifier of callee g (g itself, or the object of a member chain).
.decl skd_root(g: node, r: node)
skd_root(g, g) :- skd_callee(g, _), kind(g, "identifier").
skd_root(g, r) :- skd_callee(g, _), kind(g, "member_expression"), field(g, "object", o), skd_root_up(o, r).
.decl skd_root_up(o: node, r: node)
skd_root_up(o, o) :- kind(o, "identifier"), field(m, "object", o), kind(m, "member_expression").
skd_root_up(o, r) :- kind(o, "member_expression"), field(o, "object", p), skd_root_up(p, r).
// skd_ident(g, f, h): callee g in f is fetcher h, its dotted text with an aliased import's root read as the name
// it imports (`loadSettings` of `getSettings as loadSettings` is getSettings), or the global fetch. A name bound
// inside f (`r.json()`), a parameter of an enclosing function and other globals (JSON, Promise, console) name none.
.decl skd_ident(g: node, f: node, h: symbol)
skd_ident(g, f, cat(x, substr(s, n, strlen(s) - n))) :- skd_callee(g, f), skd_root(g, r), ref_site(r, sp),
    import_binding(sp, _, _, x), x != "*", x != "default", text(r, rt), n = strlen(rt), skd_path(g, s).
skd_ident(g, f, s) :- skd_callee(g, f), skd_root(g, r), ref_site(r, sp), !skd_named_import(sp), !within(sp, f),
    !site_form(sp, "param"), skd_path(g, s).
skd_ident(g, f, "fetch") :- skd_callee(g, f), skd_root(g, r), !ref_site(r, _), text(g, "fetch").
.decl skd_named_import(sp: node)
skd_named_import(sp) :- import_binding(sp, _, _, x), x != "*", x != "default".
// skd_path(g, s): the callee's dotted text.
.decl skd_path(g: node, s: symbol)
skd_path(g, s) :- skd_callee(g, _), name(g, s).
skd_path(g, s) :- skd_callee(g, _), !name(g, _), text(g, s).
// skd_param(f): f calls a parameter of an enclosing function (a wrapper's fetcher): unknown.
.decl skd_param(f: node)
skd_param(f) :- skd_callee(g, f), skd_root(g, r), ref_site(r, site), !within(site, f), site_form(site, "param").

// skd_fetcher(o, h): definition o reaches fetcher h, in its queryFn or one hop away. skd_arg(o, h, u): a call of h
// whose first argument is the string u (templates with `*`); skd_open(o, h): a call of h whose first argument is
// not a string.
.decl skd_scope(o: node, f: node)
skd_scope(o, f) :- skd_site(o), skd_prop(o, "queryFn", f).
skd_scope(o, def) :- skd_site(o), skd_prop(o, "queryFn", f), skd_hop(f, def).
.decl skd_fetcher(o: node, h: symbol)
skd_fetcher(o, h) :- skd_scope(o, f), skd_callee(g, f), skd_ident(g, f, h).
.decl skd_call(o: node, h: symbol, c: node)
skd_call(o, h, c) :- skd_scope(o, f), skd_callee(g, f), skd_ident(g, f, h), field(c, "function", g),
    kind(c, "call_expression").
.decl skd_first(c: node, a: node)
skd_first(c, a) :- skd_call(_, _, c), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, a, i), !kind(a, "comment"),
    count : { child(al, x, j), j < i, !kind(x, "comment") } = 0.
.decl skd_str(a: node, u: symbol)
skd_str(a, u) :- skd_first(_, a), (kind(a, "string") ; kind(a, "template_string")), str(a, u).
skd_str(a, u) :- skd_first(_, a), kind(a, "template_string"), !str(a, _), text(a, s),
    u = @replace_all(@replace_all(s, "\\$\\{[^}]*\\}", "*"), "^`|`$", "").
.decl skd_arg(o: node, h: symbol, u: symbol)
skd_arg(o, h, u) :- skd_call(o, h, c), skd_first(c, a), skd_str(a, u).
.decl skd_open(o: node, h: symbol)
skd_open(o, h) :- skd_call(o, h, c), !skd_first(c, _).
skd_open(o, h) :- skd_call(o, h, c), skd_first(c, a), !skd_str(a, _).
skd_open(o, h) :- skd_fetcher(o, h), skd_prop(o, "queryFn", f), skd_callee(f, f).

// ---- pairs -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// skd_ready(o, t, k, pk): a definition with a template, a known fetcher and no parameter call, in package pk. A
// server prefetch for hydration (skd_hydrating) is none.
.decl skd_ready(o: node, t: symbol, k: symbol, pk: symbol)
skd_ready(o, t, k, pk) :- skd_key(o, t), skd_kind(o, k), skd_fetcher(o, _), skd_prop(o, "queryFn", f), !skd_param(f),
    !skd_hydrating(o), docof(o, d), doc(d, p, _), package_for(p, pk), skd_tq_dep(pk).
// skd_hydrating(o): o is the options object of a prefetch call (`queryClient.fetchQuery({ … })`) in a file that
// calls dehydrate of a TanStack Query package (named, renamed, or `RQ.dehydrate` of a namespace import).
.decl skd_hydrating(o: node)
skd_hydrating(o) :- skd_site(o), child(al, o, _), kind(al, "arguments"), field(c, "arguments", al),
    field(c, "function", g), kind(g, "member_expression"), field(g, "property", pr), text(pr, x),
    (x = "fetchQuery" ; x = "prefetchQuery" ; x = "ensureQueryData" ; x = "fetchInfiniteQuery" ;
    x = "prefetchInfiniteQuery" ; x = "ensureInfiniteQueryData"), docof(o, d), skd_dehydrates(d).
.decl skd_dehydrates(d: number)
skd_dehydrates(d) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", g), kind(g, "identifier"), ref_site(g, sp),
    import_binding(sp, _, m, "dehydrate"), glob("{@tanstack/*query*,react-query}", m), docof(c, d).
skd_dehydrates(d) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", g), kind(g, "member_expression"),
    field(g, "property", pr), text(pr, "dehydrate"), field(g, "object", n), kind(n, "identifier"), ref_site(n, sp),
    import_binding(sp, _, m, "*"), glob("{@tanstack/*query*,react-query}", m), docof(c, d).
// skd_tq_dep(dir): the package in dir (its package.json) depends on TanStack Query (any `@tanstack/*query*` package,
// v3's `react-query`) or tRPC's React Query integration; `{ queryKey, queryFn }` objects elsewhere are not its queries.
.decl skd_tq_dep(dir: symbol)
skd_tq_dep(dir) :- package_field(dir, k, _),
    match("(dependencies|devDependencies|peerDependencies)/(@tanstack~1[a-z0-9-]*query[a-z0-9-]*|react-query|@trpc~1(react-query|tanstack-react-query|next))", k).
// skd_at(o, p, l): definition o is the one at path p whose queryFn starts on line l, the name the pairing knows it
// by. skd_def, skd_fetcher_at, skd_arg_at and skd_open_at state what the pairing reads of it under that name.
.decl skd_at(o: node, p: symbol, l: number)
skd_at(o, p, l) :- skd_ready(o, _, _, _), skd_prop(o, "queryFn", f), line(f, l), docof(o, d), doc(d, p, _).
.decl skd_def(p: symbol, l: number, t: symbol, k: symbol, pk: symbol)
skd_def(p, l, t, k, pk) :- skd_ready(o, t, k, pk), skd_at(o, p, l).
.decl skd_fetcher_at(p: symbol, l: number, h: symbol)
skd_fetcher_at(p, l, h) :- skd_at(o, p, l), skd_fetcher(o, h).
.decl skd_arg_at(p: symbol, l: number, h: symbol, u: symbol)
skd_arg_at(p, l, h, u) :- skd_at(o, p, l), skd_arg(o, h, u).
.decl skd_open_at(p: symbol, l: number, h: symbol)
skd_open_at(p, l, h) :- skd_at(o, p, l), skd_open(o, h).
// skd_pair(a, la, b, lb): two definitions of one package with one template and kind, in two files or on two lines.
.decl skd_pair(a: symbol, la: number, b: symbol, lb: number) cross_file
skd_pair(a, la, b, lb) :- skd_def(a, la, t, k, pk), skd_def(b, lb, t, k, pk), a != b.
skd_pair(a, la, a, lb) :- skd_def(a, la, t, k, pk), skd_def(a, lb, t, k, pk), la != lb.
// skd_shared(a, la, b, lb): a and b reach a common fetcher, and do not call it with different strings only.
.decl skd_shared(a: symbol, la: number, b: symbol, lb: number) cross_file
skd_shared(a, la, b, lb) :- skd_pair(a, la, b, lb), skd_fetcher_at(a, la, h), skd_fetcher_at(b, lb, h),
    !skd_apart(a, la, b, lb, h).
.decl skd_apart(a: symbol, la: number, b: symbol, lb: number, h: symbol) cross_file
skd_apart(a, la, b, lb, h) :- skd_pair(a, la, b, lb), skd_fetcher_at(a, la, h), skd_fetcher_at(b, lb, h),
    !skd_open_at(a, la, h), !skd_open_at(b, lb, h), count : { skd_arg_at(a, la, h, u), skd_arg_at(b, lb, h, u) } = 0.
.decl skd_conflict(a: symbol, la: number, b: symbol, lb: number)
skd_conflict(a, la, b, lb) :- skd_pair(a, la, b, lb), !skd_shared(a, la, b, lb).
// skd_other(a, la, b, lb): the conflict a's finding names: the first by path, then by line.
.decl skd_other(a: symbol, la: number, b: symbol, lb: number)
skd_other(a, la, b, lb) :- skd_conflict(a, la, b, lb), !skd_later(a, la, b, lb).
.decl skd_later(a: symbol, la: number, b: symbol, lb: number)
skd_later(a, la, b, lb) :- skd_conflict(a, la, b, lb), skd_conflict(a, la, b2, lb2), (b2 < b ; b2 = b, lb2 < lb).

